---
import AccountGroups from "../../components/nova/xf/AccountGroups.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { accessGroups, accessSources } from "../../data/groups";
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const global=accessGroups.filter(x=>x.scope==="Global");
const local=accessGroups.filter(x=>x.scope==="Domain Local");
---
<BaseLayout title="Company security groups" description="Explore 11 company-created Active Directory groups, direct identity membership, group nesting and separate file permissions." breadcrumbs={[{label:"Directory",href:"directory/"},{label:"Security groups"}]}>
<section class="page-head"><div class="container">
<div class="eyebrow">Identity / Access groups</div>
<h1>People join groups. Groups receive permissions.</h1>
<p class="lead" style="margin-top:17px">Department membership and folder permissions are kept apart. Follow a department group into a resource group and then into the folder's SMB and NTFS rules.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container"><AccountGroups /></div></section>
<section class="section compact"><div class="container">
  <div class="paper panel" style="margin-bottom:32px"><p class="kicker">Why two group layers?</p><h2 style="margin:12px 0 15px">Accounts → Global → Domain Local → Permissions</h2><p class="muted">This is the AGDLP pattern: I change one group instead of editing every folder. Only a real sign-in test proves the access, and I ran one for Moyo (IT allowed, Finance denied).</p><a class="evidence-link" href={base+"people/moyo/"}>Follow Moyo's verified IT path →</a></div>
  <div class="section-heading"><h2>Department membership groups</h2><span class="muted">Five Global groups</span></div>
  <div class="card-list">{global.map(g=><a class="system-card" href={base+"groups/"+g.slug+"/"}><small>Global Security group</small><h3>{g.name}</h3><p>{g.description}</p><span class="readmore">See direct members and nesting →</span></a>)}</div>
  <div class="section-heading" style="margin-top:48px"><h2>Resource permission groups</h2><span class="muted">Six Domain Local groups</span></div>
  <div class="card-list">{local.map(g=><a class="system-card" href={base+"groups/"+g.slug+"/"}><small>Domain Local · {g.shareRight} / {g.ntfsRight}</small><h3>{g.name}</h3><p>{g.description}</p><span class="readmore">Open the associated share →</span></a>)}</div>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top:24px"><strong>Full directory scope:</strong> The recorded Active Directory contains 62 security groups, of which 11 were created specifically for this company access model. The remaining 51 built-in/default groups are available in the <a href={accessSources.membership}>technical directory record</a>. They are not ones I created.</div>
</div></section>
</BaseLayout>
